  "title": "AGPC 0.3.0-41 native SSH host-key candidate",
  "notes": "AGPC 0.3.0-41 is a native Linux host-public-key registration candidate containing Core 0.3.0-34, MoteD 3.6.0-7 and Mote Proxy 2.0.0-9, with the remaining exact package bytes retained from aggregate 0.3.0-40.\n\nThe installer validates the ED25519 public file and verifies that the local SSH listener proves possession of its key. MoteD registers the public identity through MoteC; strict Proxy resolution supplies a managed, verified SSH host identity. Private keys stay on the host. A changed key remains pending the authorized S Channel decision.\n\nThe exact merged-main client artifacts passed native CI, public-content and ABI audits. Core passes installer/package tests and actual OpenSSH signature checks, including the privileged port-22 namespace fixture. Existing CX-Mesh successor handling, MoteChatD retirement through Redis-backed uchatd, SSH configuration and host keys are preserved. AGPC uses native packages; this candidate adds no Docker or ag-net requirement.\n\nThis candidate does not activate global AGPC installer URLs or signed stable APT. Device registration/resolve and S Channel authority must be explicitly enrolled before fleet activation; absent authority remains denied. Native cohort installation and live fleet acceptance are separate gates. Older native preview package lineages and Windows implementation are outside this Linux candidate.\n",
